WEBVTT

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:33.160
All right, I win five days' worth of dinner. Sorry about that!

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:34.690
Hold it!

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.390
You cheated, didn't you?

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.560
What are you saying, eh!?

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.950
Sometimes you win, sometimes you lose.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:44.400
If you'll excuse me, I'll take a look at these cards.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.450
Examine them closely!

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.550
Don't underestimate me!

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.990
Look, all right; if I was cheating then you guys can have my—

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.180
Keep it down, you guys!

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.870
Why are you squabbling over just five dinners? Have you no shame?

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.750
Can't you just be quiet and let me think?

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.650
<i>Okay, now tuck in your chin!</i>

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:25.830
<i>Old man!</i>

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.730
<i>Aoyama-kun, let's go.</i>

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.330
<i>R-Right!</i>

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.130
<i>What happened?</i>

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:45.960
I won again.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.850
I lost so badly.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.440
What are you looking at us with that stupid grin on your face for?

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.850
I lost really badly...

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.860
Didn't you hear me tell you to keep it down, you idiots!?

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.210
The shame of a man's lifetime.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.490
From what I've heard, he's sort of in a love triangle.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:14.840
A love triangle? What's that?

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.640
Well, everyone, listen up for a second!

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.630
All right!

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.670
I see now!

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.420
That Aoyama, huh?

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.680
Well, that's unfortunate for Joe.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.920
Well, let's be friendly cell mates. Let's go comfort him.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.180
Yo, Yabuki, buddy! I completely understand how you feel.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.060
I heard that one-eyed old guy gave up on you.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.570
That aside, you're representing our cell block for the boxing tournament.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.770
Shouldn't you head over to the training room

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:45.870
to practice boxing like all your competitors?

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.700
Your fists won't stay sharp if you just stay in that moldy futon!

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.900
You say my fists won't stay sharp!?

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:20.200
Sorry, but my fists don't dull that easily if I stop training!

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.160
Yabuki, buddy, take a look out there!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.180
Faster!

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.630
That one-eyed old man is pretty enthusiastic!

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.140
He came all this way even though it's not the weekend!

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.980
All for whom? For Aoyama!

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.980
I feel so much safer with him out of the room.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:08.270
All right, back to our game!

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.650
That's right. Good!

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.160
Keep your chin tucked in.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.160
You're doing well, Aoyama-kun. Keep it that way!

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:57.160
Yeah, that's it!

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.010
There! And there!

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.000
Old man!

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.900
No, no, don't do it like that!

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:07.970
Old man!

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:18.740
Why didn't you tell me you'd be here?

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.810
If I'd known, I would have come immediately!

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.610
What exactly went wrong, old man!?

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.820
Hey, Aoyama-kun!

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:28.530
Yes!

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.220
What are you doing? Carry on with your training!

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.320
Yes!

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.290
Yeah, that's right. Yup, yup, that's it!

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.610
Stop it, old man.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.500
Why are you just training Aoyama and treating me like some ugly step-sister?

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:44.920
Concentrate on your footwork!

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.900
Old man, I'm swallowing my pride and begging you.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.200
Please be my coach!

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.780
Please, I'll do anything you ask me to do.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:21.130
I beg you, please carry on with my training!

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:26.300
I love boxing,

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.990
and for my next match with Rikiishi...

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:31.570
I really don't want to lose to him!

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:38.140
Aren't you getting ahead of yourself, Joe?

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:44.270
No matter what you say, my hands are full coaching Aoyama.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.650
I have to ask you to stop bothering us.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:49.780
Old man!

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:53.230
Aoyama-kun, we can't keep training now that we've been interrupted.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.310
Let's go somewhere else.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:55.020
Yes.

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:15.860
A stray dog, abandoned by its master, becomes miserably pathetic, huh?

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:22.060
Why did that old man suddenly give him the cold shoulder?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.490
I really don't know.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:27.430
Yabuki probably pissed him off somehow.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.230
Yeah, sounds about right.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.430
<i>You'll be boxing with me!</i>

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.540
<i>You'll always be mine, Joe!</i>

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.020
All right!

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:41.850
In that case, I won't ask old man Danpei to coach me anymore!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:43.890
Not even if he comes to me and begs!

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.920
The old man and Joe...

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:53.210
Something is going on with them. Something...

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:58.470
That's right, I feel like a burning flame is raging between them.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:03.640
I can't put my finger on the cause, but if I don't tread carefully,

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:09.570
I'll get burned by that faint, yet hot and fierce flame!

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:27.940
Th-This is serious!

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:28.920
Terrible!

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:31.770
Someone get the doctor down here from the infirmary!

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:34.820
What, what? What happened?

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.320
What's that about getting the doctor? Was there another fight!?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.020
It wasn't a fight! Hurry up and call the doctor!

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.110
Numata...

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:45.470
Numata's been beaten up pretty badly. If we don't help him now...

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.690
Guards, please get over here!

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:49.230
Hey, did you hear that?

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:55.340
Someone destroyed Numata. He was supposed to represent block seven in the boxing tournament!

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.080
What!? It's <i>that</i> Numata!?

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:58.030
What a surprise!

00:10:58.030 --> 00:10:59.870
Who was his opponent?

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:02.790
Well, that's... It seems like it was Aoyama!

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:04.300
Aoyama, you say?

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:08.310
L-Look at him... He's messed up!

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.820
A-Aoyama!?

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.770
I-It's true!

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.870
That anemic Aoyama has...

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.870
<i>What happened here?</i>

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:29.840
I-It wasn't a fight. It wasn't a fight!

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:32.600
We had a match to decide who'd represent the cell block.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:37.690
I wanted to be the representative no matter what, so Numata-san challenged me for the position.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:43.370
Th-Then we fought, and before I knew it, Numata-san was lying on the floor in a pool of blood.

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:45.850
What should I do now?

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:23.580
Huh? Aoyama has...

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:25.590
You can't judge a book by its cover.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:28.700
This is so unbelievable...

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.700
<i>What the hell happened here!?</i>

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:34.190
What did Aoyama do? Did anyone here see what happened!?

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:44.210
What happened!?

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.320
Tell me! What did Aoyama do to Numata!?

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:47.070
I can't breathe!

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.610
Why are you so upset, Joe!?

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:49.760
What!?

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.020
He can't talk if you're roughing him up like that!

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.270
Let him go!

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:57.280
You're right.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:02.770
All right, let's hear it! Play it back for me.

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:05.740
What did Aoyama do to Numata, eh!?

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.810
Well, that's... He was taken down when we weren't looking.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:12.830
Wh-What!?

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:18.990
Well, we all knew that Aoyama was going to be part of the cell block's five-man boxing team,

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:23.390
but Numata said Aoyama would have to beat him to be the representative.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.570
Aoyama-san.

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:30.930
You're the champ!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.990
Do your best!

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.180
Please go easy on me.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.540
Yes, that's good.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.140
But let me tell you, Aoyama, it's too late now.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.650
Prepare yourself and come at me!

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:43.150
Well then, Round One!

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:46.120
What's wrong? What's wrong!? Come!

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:49.190
Oh, no... Don't mind me.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:51.200
Well, then I'll just start this myself!

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.360
It's decided!

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:52.950
Just as expected!

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:59.290
Oh! That weakling is doing well, dodging all these punches!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:01.120
You bastard!

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.880
As if he was some konjac pudding!

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:24.650
He kept dodging all the punches as if he were some konjac pudding.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.770
That's right.

00:15:26.770 --> 00:15:30.710
I wondered how long the fight would last. I got bored watching them.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:33.510
We thought playing shougi would be more interesting than that boring fight...

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:36.660
...so we had another shougi tournament.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:40.660
Anyway, when we looked up again, Numata was on the floor, covered in blood,

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:43.680
while Aoyama was standing beside him like a ghost.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:00.450
Joe, I think you only have one option left.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.670
Why don't you go ask Aoyama yourself?

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:08.070
Wait a second, Joe!

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.510
Ask Aoyama?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.030
How ridiculous!

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.400
Joe, what's wrong?

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.450
Why not ask Aoyama-kun?

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.730
What am I supposed to ask him? And how?

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:38.120
Why are you deceiving yourself?

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:42.690
You've begun to see the truth, so why are you looking away from it?

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.560
Me? What have I begun to see?

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:51.840
Aoyama defeated Numata.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.930
He knocked him down, covered in blood!

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:57.070
How annoying. So what's the matter with that!?

00:16:58.090 --> 00:17:01.280
You're trying to tell yourself that it was a fluke.

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:03.170
You're panicking and trying to ignore what happened.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.310
Stop making stuff up!

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:09.110
I understand.

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:11.030
Numata underestimated Aoyama.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.010
He just swung at Aoyama's face with sloppy footwork.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.580
He lowered his guard because it was Aoyama, then he had to face the consequences.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:21.460
Numata was completely ridiculed by Aoyama. What a slob!

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:27.460
You heard this part too, right?

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:31.790
Numata was trying to finish Aoyama right away. He was attacking him relentlessly.

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:38.530
<i>Y-You bastard!</i>

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.580
<i>You...</i>

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:01.280
Joe!

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.520
Numata didn't fight Aoyama with his hands and feet tied, now did he?

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:43.340
Aoyama!

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.030
Aoyama!

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:01.230
Answer me.

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:03.200
What did you do to Numata?

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.590
I'm asking what you did to him!

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:15.280
What I did?

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:19.860
Like I said before, I just did what coach Danpei taught me!

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.410
And just what did Danpei teach you?

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:27.210
What strategy did he teach you!? You son of a...

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:30.900
I-Isn't it weird to be asking me that, Yabuki-san?

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:35.100
O-Ouch, that hurts! Please take your hand off me!

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:36.860
Th-That bastard...

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:41.880
I'm sorry I can't tell you, but as a representative of cell block seven,

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:45.020
I might end up facing you in the tournament.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:53.710
Telling a potential opponent my secrets is like saying I'll use a rock in rock-paper-scissors.

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:55.260
You bastard!

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:57.130
P-Please stop it!

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:03.640
Yabuki-san, you're just upset that coach Danpei is only teaching me!

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:05.140
Isn't that right!?

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.430
D-Damn...

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.110
But that isn't my fault.

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:12.490
Coach Danpei decided to teach me. I'm just doing as he says.

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:14.930
In other words, I'm just passive in this.

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:19.020
Passive!?

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:22.400
I guess he taught you how to talk, not just how to box.

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:24.750
That's not it!

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:28.070
In other words, if you hate and despise me that much,

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:31.410
at least show it in the ring!

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:37.420
A-Are you saying that you want to be my opponent in the ring?

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:40.420
Uh, well...

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.960
You surprised me.

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:47.340
Well, instead of waiting for the tournament, how about we fight right here!?

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.400
Hold it!

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:01.370
Looks like you've lost, Yabuki.

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:04.220
What?

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:13.360
I thought you'd just walk away after Aoyama cut you so deep, but you stray dog...

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:18.330
You shamelessly unleash your fangs to take away what he holds dearest.

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:20.930
How shameful, Yabuki!

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:26.310
Just wait for this match to be settled in the ring.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:35.350
I have a good idea of what your coach taught Aoyama.

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:43.360
It's nothing I need to worry about, but... it's going to be a tough fight for you.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.370
Shut up!

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:47.410
I'm the guy you had a draw with!

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.960
Look, for me to be taken down by the likes of Aoyama—

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:53.410
Hold it! I wonder about that.

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:58.420
I think I understand what's going on in your head right now.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:02.920
Aoyama's presence, which wasn't even noticeable before,

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:07.430
is slowly but surely increasing.

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:10.260
Isn't that right, Yabuki?

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:49.930
Regardless of what happens, I'm still hoping to fight you again.

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:54.490
Make sure you don't get beaten up by Aoyama or anyone else before I get my chance.

00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:40.720
The prison's boxing tournament has begun.

00:24:40.720 --> 00:24:43.200
Aoyama, who has become a threatening opponent,

00:24:43.590 --> 00:24:47.080
wins match after match with the advanced techniques I taught him.

00:24:47.630 --> 00:24:51.670
Joe's spirit ignites as he sees Aoyama win his matches.

00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:57.010
Now, for Joe, who is ravaged by sadness inside the ropes, which way is tomorrow!?
